PUPIL PREMIUM
What is Pupil Premium?
Pupil Premium is additional funding provided by the government to improve outcomes for disadvantaged pupils. It is allocated to schools based on the number of pupils who are eligible for free school meals, have been eligible in the past six years, are looked after by the local authority, or have parents serving in the armed forces.
We are committed to ensuring that all pupils, regardless of background or circumstance, have equal access to a high-quality education. We use our Pupil Premium funding to remove barriers to learning and to support pupils to achieve as well as their peers.
